      "side": 1,
      "message": "The hash is stable across regens, but it is not distinct: with `cloud01..cloud12`, `cloud02`/`cloud03` land 5.6 degrees apart and `cloud01`/`cloud09`, `cloud04`/`cloud10`, `cloud05`/`cloud06` 7.1 degrees apart at the same S/L, so those legend swatches read as the same color (the old 10-color palette was distinct up to 10 clouds). Hashing into a wider perceptually spaced palette, or snapping to well-separated buckets with a deterministic offset for duplicates, keeps stability and separates them. `hashlib.sha1(..., usedforsecurity\u003dFalse)` also keeps this working on FIPS-enabled hosts, since the hue is not a security digest. At hue 60-90 the fixed 38% lightness gives 2.9-3.3:1 against white, so the deferred contrast item is unchanged.",
      "revId": "9015e6e900517f37aca3d55ebfa390f6868ff372",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
